{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope/Grounding: The answer says the treatment causes a \"14.4 percentage point decrease\" yet the computed difference is positive (0.1436), indicating an increase, not a decrease.",
    "Overreach: The answer presents the adjusted difference as a causal \"treatment effect\" despite the data being non‑randomised and only adjusting for severity; residual confounding remains.",
    "Unacknowledged data problem: Weighting by the overall severity distribution (which is heavily skewed toward mild cases) may not yield an unbiased estimate of the effect for the target population, and this limitation is not discussed."
  ]
}
